Fixed the backend image failing to create a site. `create_site.py` applied `pas.plugins.identity:initial` whenever `EXAMPLE_CONTENT` was set, which it is by default, and this package registers no such profile — so `docker run -e SITE=Plone` died with `KeyError` after the site had already been created, reporting a GenericSetup problem rather than an example-content one. The profile is now applied only when it is actually registered, which keeps the hook for whenever it arrives. @ericof
